WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.875
Crypto agility is the ability to change cryptographic algorithms, keys, libraries, and protocols without redesigning an entire system.

2
00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:12.137
It is not a slogan; it is an architectural property.

3
00:00:12.137 --> 00:00:29.964
A crypto-agile system avoids hard-coded assumptions, keeps algorithms configurable where appropriate, supports versioned protocol negotiation, separates policy from implementation, and gives teams a realistic way to test and deploy changes without emergency rewrites.

4
00:00:29.964 --> 00:00:32.467
Prioritization should be risk-based.

5
00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:46.046
Systems protecting sensitive data with a long confidentiality lifetime deserve early attention, especially if they are exposed to untrusted networks or depend on public-key encryption and key establishment.

6
00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:53.859
Operationally critical systems also need careful planning because outages can be more damaging than delayed migration.

7
00:00:53.859 --> 00:00:56.438
Dependency complexity matters as well.

8
00:00:56.438 --> 00:01:05.996
A service may be ready internally but blocked by a client library, partner integration, hardware module, certificate authority, or vendor product.

9
00:01:05.996 --> 00:01:09.410
Hybrid approaches may appear during the transition.

10
00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:20.561
Conceptually, a hybrid design combines an existing mechanism with a post-quantum mechanism so the system can manage interoperability and risk while the ecosystem matures.

11
00:01:20.561 --> 00:01:27.616
Hybrid does not mean automatically safer in every implementation, and it does not remove the need for testing.

12
00:01:27.616 --> 00:01:37.326
It is a migration strategy that must be evaluated in the context of protocols, libraries, performance, failure behavior, and operational visibility.

13
00:01:37.326 --> 00:01:40.588
A practical plan uses pilots before broad rollout.

14
00:01:40.588 --> 00:01:53.332
Teams test interoperability, measure performance, review logging, validate monitoring, confirm certificate and key lifecycle behavior, coordinate with vendors, and define fallback criteria.

15
00:01:53.332 --> 00:01:58.794
The danger is a rushed replacement that breaks systems or silently weakens security.

16
00:01:58.794 --> 00:02:07.972
A disciplined migration creates decision records, tracks readiness, and moves high-risk use cases forward while keeping production stable.
